      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nAn unfinished chunk checkpoint reconstructs the full tree index path and writes the request row even when insertion adopted the request's existing indices unchanged. Skip that redundant work when the matched prefix does not extend beyond the already protected prefix.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\nKeep the existing rebinding path for newly duplicated prefixes, finished requests and session caching. Preserve full inserted-length protection for SWA tombstones and retain the early return for rotation-tail rejection. This covers unfinished chunks; #43600 separately optimizes finished-request bookkeeping.\r\n\r\nAdd regression coverage for unshared inserts, successive chunks and duplicate-prefix adoption.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n| Run order | Baseline (µs/chunk) | Candidate (µs/chunk) |\r\n|---|---:|---:|\r\n| A1 / B1 | 491.44 | 398.04 |\r\n| A2 / B2 | 602.60 | 400.47 |\r\n| A3 / B3 | 500.23 | 410.31 |\r\n\r\n### CI States\r\n\r\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39636860822](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39636860822)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39636860504](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39636860504)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39636860711](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39636860711)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\r\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
